    {
      "file": "src/md4c.c",
      "function": "md_parse",
      "line": 6320,
      "code": "ctx.text = text;\n    ctx.size = size;",
      "note": "First non-harness project statement that materializes the parser-visible input span. After the harness consumes its two 4-byte flag words, md4c stores a pointer to the remaining Markdown slice and its length in `ctx`.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/md4c.c",
      "function": "md_is_container_mark",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if(off > beg  &&\n       (CH(off) == _T('.') || CH(off) == _T(')'))  &&\n       (off+1 >= ctx->size || ISBLANK(off+1) || ISNEWLINE(off+1)))",
      "note": "After ordered-list digit scanning advances `off` to the end of the document, this condition checks only `off > beg` before dereferencing `CH(off)` to look for `'.'` or `')'`. When the digit run reaches the document boundary, `off == ctx->size`, so the delimiter probe itself is out of bounds. The patch fixes this exact obligation by inserting `off < ctx->size` before `CH(off)`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
